1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,220
In twenty seventeen, police cameras in Cardiff raised two thousand four hundred seventy watch-list alerts.

2
00:00:07,520 --> 00:00:08,900
What percent were right?

3
00:00:09,200 --> 00:00:10,170
Pick a number.

4
00:00:11,833 --> 00:00:14,373
Each alert is a positive test result.

5
00:00:14,773 --> 00:00:17,513
One in five hundred people has this disease.

6
00:00:17,813 --> 00:00:23,703
A test catches ninety-nine percent of the sick and wrongly flags one percent of the healthy.

7
00:00:24,103 --> 00:00:27,163
If yours says positive, what's the chance you're sick?

8
00:00:29,100 --> 00:00:34,170
At one Boston-area hospital, doctors and students got a problem like this.

9
00:00:34,570 --> 00:00:38,020
Their most common answer was the test's own accuracy:

10
00:00:38,320 --> 00:00:39,810
ninety-five percent.

11
00:00:40,410 --> 00:00:44,090
For our test, that's ninety-nine: you'd start treatment today.

12
00:00:44,533 --> 00:00:48,773
Check that rule by counting: ten thousand people, half of them sick.

13
00:00:49,233 --> 00:00:51,653
Test everyone, and watch who lights up.

14
00:00:52,700 --> 00:00:56,630
Of the five thousand who lit up, ninety-nine percent are sick.

15
00:00:56,930 --> 00:00:58,410
Here, the rule holds.

16
00:00:58,866 --> 00:01:05,396
Now keep the same test, and make the disease rarer and rarer, down to yours: one in five hundred.

17
00:01:06,300 --> 00:01:11,840
About twenty sick people light up, plus one percent of everyone else: about a hundred.

18
00:01:12,433 --> 00:01:16,023
So of a hundred twenty positives, only twenty are sick.

19
00:01:16,233 --> 00:01:17,723
Seventeen percent.

20
00:01:18,866 --> 00:01:20,596
The rule said ninety-nine.

21
00:01:20,796 --> 00:01:22,376
Six times too high.

22
00:01:23,366 --> 00:01:28,076
One percent sounds small, but here it's one percent of nearly everyone.

23
00:01:28,533 --> 00:01:33,083
Your positive result ruled out everyone who tested negative.

24
00:01:33,700 --> 00:01:38,500
What's left is a smaller sample space: these hundred twenty people.

25
00:01:38,966 --> 00:01:41,786
Your chance is the red share of this crowd.

26
00:01:43,733 --> 00:01:52,643
Unrounded, the red count is twenty sick people times ninety-nine percent, and the blue, every healthy person times one percent.

27
00:01:53,233 --> 00:01:57,133
Divide everything by ten thousand: counts become shares.

28
00:01:57,533 --> 00:01:59,063
The share stays the same.

29
00:02:00,100 --> 00:02:02,110
These are how common each group is,

30
00:02:02,410 --> 00:02:05,340
and these are how often each group tests positive.

31
00:02:05,640 --> 00:02:07,850
Name them, and you have Bayes' theorem.

32
00:02:08,300 --> 00:02:13,590
All it does is shrink the sample space to what the evidence allows, then take the share.

33
00:02:14,933 --> 00:02:17,413
Swap the disease for a police watch list.

34
00:02:17,866 --> 00:02:23,966
About a hundred seventy thousand people came, and the watch lists held about twelve hundred photos.

35
00:02:24,700 --> 00:02:28,380
For four days, face-recognition cameras scanned the crowds.

36
00:02:28,680 --> 00:02:31,140
Every face they flagged joined the alerts.

37
00:02:31,533 --> 00:02:32,893
Shrink to the alerts.

38
00:02:33,293 --> 00:02:34,473
Take the red share.

39
00:02:34,813 --> 00:02:39,323
The police counted a hundred seventy-three as right: seven percent.

40
00:02:40,766 --> 00:02:43,826
In machine learning, that share is called precision.

41
00:02:44,866 --> 00:02:51,286
Cardiff University's evaluators counted only alerts the logbooks confirmed: three percent.

42
00:02:51,786 --> 00:02:56,536
Months later, a new algorithm and better photos cut the false alarms.

43
00:02:57,136 --> 00:02:59,666
That's the blue term in Bayes' denominator.

44
00:02:59,966 --> 00:03:02,316
Their count rose to forty-six percent.

45
00:03:03,366 --> 00:03:04,586
Back to your test.

46
00:03:06,713 --> 00:03:15,313
Symptoms raise the one in five hundred: at one in a hundred, fifty percent; at one in two, ninety-nine, where the rule held.

47
00:03:16,666 --> 00:03:23,926
That ninety-nine percent, the test's accuracy, is also its recall: how often the sick test positive.

48
00:03:24,226 --> 00:03:28,126
Seventeen percent describes your result: its precision.

49
00:03:28,833 --> 00:03:30,823
Your test didn't say you're sick.

50
00:03:31,223 --> 00:03:33,333
It said: you're in this crowd.

